{"step_index":173,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:39:40Z","thinking":"**Relating Walk Length to Ball Membership**\n\nA bypass in a walk is a path, and its length is no greater than the original walk's length. Since a connected graph implies a walk between any two vertices, a path of finite length must exist between them. This path's length is bounded by the number of vertices in the graph minus one.\n\nConsidering a walk from vertex `v` to `w` of length at most `k`, the question is whether `w` belongs to the ball of radius `k` centered at `v`.\n\n\n**Formulating the Walk Lemma**\n\nThe central claim is, if there's a walk `p` from `v` to `w`, then `w` is in the ball of radius `p.length` centered at `v`.  Induction on `p` seems appropriate. The base case, `Walk.nil`, is straightforward.  `Walk.cons` adds an edge at the *beginning* of the walk, which complicates the induction.\n\nReconsidering: Induction on the *length* of the walk might be more natural, or using `Walk.reverse` for induction might be required. Checking if there's `Walk.concat` in the existing environment. Also, considering a potential helper lemma.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python -c '\nimport glob\nfor p in glob.glob(\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/lean_project/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/Combinatorics/SimpleGraph/**/*.lean\", recursive=True):\n    with open(p) as f:\n        txt = f.read()\n    if \"reverse_induction\" in txt or \"concat\" in txt:\n        for line in txt.splitlines():\n            if (\"reverse_induction\" in line or \"concat\" in line) and (\"theorem\" in line or \"def\" in line or \"lemma\" in line):\n                print(line)\n'","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Searching for concat in Mathlib Walk","toolSummary":"Search Walk concat"}}]}
