emma ballWithin_subset_succ {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n101:     (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (k : ℕ) (v : V) :\n102:     ballWithin G k v ⊆ ballWithin G (k + 1) v := by\n103:   intro x hx\n104:   dsimp [ballWithin]\n105:   exact Finset.mem_union_left _ hx\n106: \n107: lemma ballWithin_subset_add {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n108:     (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (k m : ℕ) (v : V) :\n109:     ballWithin G k v ⊆ ballWithin G (k + m) v := by\n110:   induction m with\n111:   | zero => exact Finset.Subset.refl _\n112:   | succ m ih =>\n113:     have h1 := ballWithin_subset_succ G (k + m) v\n114:     exact Finset.Subset.trans ih h1\n115: \n116: lemma ballWithin_succ_eq_self_implies_add {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n117:     (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (k : ℕ) (v : V)\n118:     (h : ballWithin G (k + 1) v = ballWithin G k v) (m : ℕ) :\n119:     ballWithin G (k + m) v = ballWithin G k v := by\n120:   induction m with\n121:   | zero => rfl\n122:   | succ m ih =>\n123:     have heq : k + (m + 1) = (k + m) + 1 := by omega\n124:     rw [heq]\n125:     dsimp [ballWithin]\n126:     rw [ih]\n127:     exact h\n128: \n129: lemma ballWithin_succ_eq_self_implies_univ {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n130:     (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (k : ℕ) (v : V)\n131:     (hrad : GraphCalc.HasRadius G)\n132:     (h : ballWithin G (k + 1) v = ballWithin G k v) :\n133:     ballWithin G k v = Finset.univ := by\n134:   have h_add := ballWithin_succ_eq_self_implies_add G k v h (Fintype.card V)\n135:   have h_sub : ballWithin G (Fintype.card V) v ⊆ ballWithin G (k + Fintype.card V) v := by\n136:     have heq : k + Fintype.card V = Fintype.card V + k := by omega\n137:     rw [heq]\n138:     exact ballWithin_subset_add G (Fintype.card V) k v\n139:   rw [hrad v] at h_sub\n140:   rw [h_add] at h_sub\n141:   ext x\n142:   exact ⟨fun _ => Finset.mem_univ x, fun _ => h_sub (Finset.mem_univ x)⟩\n143: \n144: lemma card_ballWithin_succ_of_ne_univ {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n145:     (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (k : ℕ) (v : V)\n146:     (hrad : GraphCalc.HasRadius G)\n147:     (hne : ballWithin G k v ≠ Finset.univ) :\n148:     (ballWithin G k v).card + 1 ≤ (ballWithin G (k + 1) v).card := by\n149:   have h_not_eq : ballWithin G (k + 1) v ≠ ballWithin G k v := by\n150:     intro heq\n151:     exact hne (ballWithin_succ_eq_self_implies_univ G k v hrad heq)\n152:   have h_sub := ballWithin_subset_succ G k v\n153:   have h_ssub : ballWithin G k v ⊂ ballWithin G (k + 1) v :=\n154:     Finset.ssubset_iff_subset_ne.mpr ⟨h_sub, h_not_eq.symm⟩\n155:   exact Finset.card_lt_card h_ssub\n156: \n157: lemma ballWithin_univ_or_card_ge {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n158:     (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V)\n159:     (hrad : GraphCalc.HasRadius G) (k : ℕ) :\n160:     ballWithin G k v = Finset.univ ∨ k + 1 ≤ (ballWithin G k v).card := by\n161:   induction k with\n162:   | zero =>\n163:     right\n164:     dsimp [ballWithin]\n165:     simp\n166:   | succ k ih =>\n167:     cases ih with\n168:     | inl h_univ =>\n169:       left\n170:       have hsub := ballWithin_subset_succ G k v\n171:       rw [h_univ] at hsub\n172:       ext x\n173:       exact ⟨fun _ => Finset.mem_univ x, fun _ => hsub (Finset.mem_univ x)⟩\n174:     | inr h_card =>\n175:       by_cases hne : ballWithin G k v = Finset.univ\n176:       · left\n177:         have hsub := ballWithin_subset_succ G k v\n178:         rw [hne] at hsub\n179:         ext x\n180:         exact ⟨fun _ => Finset.mem_univ x, fun _ => hsub (Finset.mem_univ x)⟩\n181:       · right\n182:         have hstep := card_ballWithin_succ_of_ne_univ G k v hrad hne\n183:         omega\n184: \n185: lemma ballWithin_card_pred_eq_univ {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n186:     (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V)\n187:     (hrad : GraphCalc.HasRadius G) (hnt : GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass G) :\n188:     ballWithin G (Fintype.card V - 1) v = Finset.univ := by\n189:   have h := ballWithin_univ_or_card_ge G v hrad (Fintype.card V - 1)\n190:   cases h with\n191:   | inl h1 => exact h1\n192:   | inr h2 =>\n193:     unfold GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass at hnt\n194:     unfold GraphCalc.order at hnt\n195:     have h_card_eq : (Fintype.card V - 1) + 1 = Fintype.card V := by omega\n196:     rw [h_card_eq] at h2\n197:     by_contra hc\n198:     have h_ssub : ballWithin G (Fintype.card V - 1) v ⊂ Finset.univ :=\n199:       Finset.ssubset_univ_iff.mpr hc\n200:     have h_lt := Finset.card_lt_card h_ssub\n201:     rw [Finset.card_univ] at h_lt\n202:     omega\n203: \n204: lemma eccentricity_le_card_pred {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n205:     (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V)\n206:     (hrad : GraphCalc.HasRadius G) (hnt : GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass G) :\n207:     GraphCalc.eccentricity G v ≤ Fintype.card V - 1 := by\n208:   unfold GraphCalc.eccentricity\n209:   unfold GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass at hnt\n210:   unfold GraphCalc.order at hnt\n211:   apply minUpTo_le (Fintype.card V - 1) (by omega) (ballWithin_card_pred_eq_univ G v hrad hnt)\n212: \n213: lemma radius_add_one_le_card {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n214:     (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n215:     (hrad : GraphCalc.HasRadius G) (hnt : GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass G) :\n216:     GraphCalc.radius G + 1 ≤ Fintype.card V := by\n217:   unfold GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass at hnt\n218:   unfold GraphCalc.order at hnt\n219:   obtain ⟨v⟩ := Fintype.card_pos_iff.mp (by omega : 0 < Fintype.card V)\n220:   have h_rad_le := radius_le_eccentricity G v\n221:   have h_ecc_le := eccentricity_le_card_pred G v hrad hnt\n222:   omega\n223: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":185,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:39:59Z","thinking":"**Reviewing prior proofs**\n\nExamining the previously established results, particularly those related to the ballWithin function and cardinality, to understand how they might be leveraged. The goal is to identify which of these previously proved lemmas can contribute to the ongoing proof effort.\n\n\n**Analyzing the current state**\n\nThe existing `radius_add_one_le_card` lemma handles the case when the roman weight is greater than or equal to the cardinality of the vertex set. The remaining challenge involves the case where the roman weight is strictly less than the cardinality, which only occurs when a vertex has value 2. Examining a related lemma, focusing on the ballWithin function's behavior to understand how this case can be handled. It is anticipated that the lemma `card_ballWithin_succ_of_ne_univ` will provide insight.\n\n\n**Evaluating the neighborhood of c**\n\nConsidering a specific vertex `c` where the function `f` evaluates to 2.  The ball of radius 1 around `c` encompasses `c` itself, and all vertices adjacent to `c`. Observing the set of vertices with function value 0, they would be neighbors of c if there's only one vertex with function value 2.\n\n**Deduction on ballWithin size**\n\nIf there is only one vertex `c` where `f c = 2`, then the set of vertices with `f(u) = 0` are all neighbors of `c`, implying this set is a subset of the ball of radius 1 around `c`. Also, `c` itself is within the ball.\n\n\n**Analyzing the ballWithin size**\n\nThe size of the set $\\{c\\} \\cup V_0$ can be calculated as $n - |V_1|$, where `n` is the total number of vertices and $|V_1| = \\text{romanWeight } f - 2$. The difference between `n` and the size of $\\{c\\} \\cup V_0$ is at most $\\text{romanWeight } f - 2$.\n\n**Deducing the maximum steps**\n\nBy the `card_ballWithin_succ_of_ne_univ` rule, at each step at least one vertex is added. After